%description:

Tcp.sendMssOption:on -- the SYN carries the MSS option.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "send the MSS option in the SYN and the SYN-ACK".

The classes: on (true, the default), off (false). The code: the MSS option goes into a SYN and
a SYN-ACK only with this flag (TcpAlgorithmBase). This test separates "on" from "off".

Host under test: host1. Observation: level 1, the SYN of host1 has an MSS option.

%# parameter: Tcp.sendMssOption
%# class: on
%# value: true
%# key: *.host1.tcp.sendMssOption
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"
#include "TcpMutations.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpSendMssOptionOn")
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
                  .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
                  .first()
                  .assertEvent([](const MatchContext& context) { return tcpMssOptionOf(context.event.packet) > 0; })
                  .describe("the SYN of host1, with an MSS option")
                  .within(0.5));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpSendMssOptionOn compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.sendMssOption = true    # the parameter under test
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpSendMssOptionOn: PASS
